  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia and Uganda Towards Implementation of the Global Compact for Migration (GCM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of the proposed action is to support the implementation of the overall objectives of the GCM for Safe, Orderly and Regular migration in Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia and Uganda. The outcome the project aims to achieve is: Strengthened capacities of governments of Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia and Uganda to increasingly mainstream migration in related policies and strategic decision-making. The three outputs of the project are: Output 1: Access to technical support, coordination fora and relevant evidence to effectively establish priorities for the implementation of the GCM and review their progress during global/regional review meetings in Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia and Uganda improved. Output 2: Skills and knowledge of key stakeholders in Djibouti, Ethiopia, Somalia and Uganda to effectively mainstream migration into priority multi-sectoral policies and strategies strengthened. Output 3: Access to resources for relevant UN coordination systems to effectively support migration mainstreaming into prioritized public policy domains, in line with the GCM, facilitated.</narrative>
  </description>
